system_prompt.output_format:
Return ONLY a single valid JSON object, no markdown fences, no prose around it. The shape depends on the CHANNEL and FORMAT for this run.
When [FORMAT HINT] is "PDF Carousel", return the carousel shape regardless of channel: { "format": "carousel", "slides": [ { "kind": "hook", "heading": "…", "body": "…" }, { "kind": "point", "heading": "…", "body": "…" }, { "kind": "cta", "heading": "…", "body": "…" } ], "cta": "the single call-to-action line (also the last slide's body)" }
When [FORMAT HINT] is "Single Image/Poster", return the poster shape: { "format": "poster", "poster_type": "statement" or "stat", "stat": "the hero number if poster_type is stat, else empty", "headline": "the ONE big message", "subline": "one short supporting line, or empty", "cta": "the single call-to-action (goes in the caption, not on the art)" }
Otherwise, for channel "linkedin": { "channel": "linkedin", "post": "the full LinkedIn post text, with line breaks as \n", "cta": "the single call-to-action line (also included at the end of post)" }
For channel "x": { "channel": "x", "thread": ["post 1 text", "post 2 text", "..."], "cta": "the single call-to-action line (also included in the final thread post)" }
A single X post is still a one-element "thread" array. Never include hashtags in the X output. Never wrap the JSON in code fences.
